# Soba Guard art prompts (sourced by the generation commands; see prompts.txt for the call log)
STYLE='Chunky 16-bit pixel art with big square pixels on a consistent coarse grid, flat colors with 3-4 shades per material, solid dark purple-black 1-pixel outline (#1a1220) around every shape, no gradients, no anti-aliasing, no texture noise. Warm lantern-lit night palette: honey wood, paper-lantern red, gold, cream, teal accents, dusty violet and plum shadows. Cute chibi proportions with big heads.'

P_SOBA="Sprite sheet of the SAME dog character as the reference images (Soba, a small fluffy black-white-and-tan dog; the first reference is the approved hero render, the second shows her approved in-game sprites). 10 poses arranged in a neat grid of 2 rows and 5 columns, with wide empty transparent gaps between poses so no two poses touch. Every pose faces RIGHT (head and nose toward the right edge of the image) and is drawn at exactly the same scale (the head is the same size in every pose), all standing on the same invisible ground line within a row. Keep every marking in every pose: black fluffy body, tall pointed upright ears with pink insides, large warm-brown eyes with a white shine pixel, tan dot above each eye, tan cheeks, thin white forehead stripe, white muzzle and black nose, big white chest ruff, white front legs and paws, tan back legs with white toes, fluffy black plumed tail curled up over the back. Render black fur as dark charcoal with a few lighter blue-grey tufts so the shape reads on a dark night background.
Row 1: (1) idle: standing on all four paws in side three-quarter view facing right, alert and happy, mouth closed, tail up. (2) idle breathing: identical pose, chest slightly raised and ears a touch taller, mouth slightly open with tongue tip. (3) bark wind-up: same stance leaning back slightly, head raised, mouth closed, ears up, determined look. (4) BARK: lunging forward to the right, front legs braced, mouth WIDE open barking, ears forward, tail stiff up. (5) cheer: sitting up on the hind legs with both front paws raised high, mouth wide open, eyes happily closed.
Row 2: (6)(7)(8)(9) a four-frame RUN cycle to the right, horizontal body, same size each: (6) front legs reaching forward, back legs pushing back; (7) legs gathered under the body, all paws close together; (8) all legs stretched apart in flight; (9) legs crossing under the body, ears streaming back. (10) sad: sitting, head low, ears drooped flat to the sides, eyes looking down, tail down, no tongue.
Same chunky low-resolution pixel-art style as the second reference: big square pixels, flat colors, 3-4 shades, solid dark purple-black 1-pixel outline, no fur noise, no anti-aliasing. Original pixel-art game character. No text, no numbers, no labels, no shadows, no ground, transparent background."

P_DEF="Game sprite sheet for a cozy Japanese noodle-house lane-defense game at night: 12 sprites in a neat grid of 4 rows and 3 columns, with wide empty transparent gaps so no two sprites touch, every sprite drawn at the same scale and standing on the same ground line in its row. Every character faces RIGHT. They are cute kitchen objects with simple faces (two big dot eyes and a small mouth). Each row is ONE character: column 1 and 2 are a two-frame idle animation (nearly identical, only a small bounce or blink), column 3 is its action frame.
Row 1, Lucky Cat: a white ceramic maneki-neko beckoning cat with red collar and gold bell, orange and black calico spots, sitting, body turned to face right. (1) raised paw up, (2) raised paw bent down mid-wave, (3) holding up a big shiny gold coin with a square hole in both paws, sparkle.
Row 2, Dumpling Steamer: a round bamboo steamer basket with a lid, on two stubby little feet, a cheerful face on the basket front, wisps of white steam on top. (4) idle, (5) idle with the steam puff shifted, (6) the lid pops up and a white dumpling launches out to the right.
Row 3, Chili Lantern: a round red paper lantern with a bold chili-pepper painted on it, gold top and bottom caps, warm inner glow, fierce little face, standing on a short wooden post. (7) idle, (8) idle with brighter glow, (9) blazing: orange glow and fiery embers bursting out to the right.
Row 4, Onigiri Wall: a big triangular white rice ball with a black nori seaweed band across the bottom, determined frowning face, sturdy and wide. (10) full and healthy, (11) a big bite taken out of one corner, grains scattered, worried face, (12) cracked and crumbling with several bites missing and pieces falling, dizzy face.
$STYLE No text, no numbers, no labels, no shadows, no ground, transparent background."

P_ENEMY="Game sprite sheet for a cozy Japanese lane-defense game at night: 20 enemy sprites in a neat grid of 5 rows and 4 columns, with wide empty transparent gaps so no two sprites touch, every sprite at the same scale, standing on the same ground line in its row. EVERY creature faces LEFT (head and nose toward the left edge of the image), walking from right to left. Cute but mischievous critters, chunky bold silhouettes that stay readable at 32 pixels. In every row: columns 1 and 2 are a two-frame WALK cycle (legs alternating), columns 3 and 4 are a two-frame BITE attack (mouth wide open lunging left, then mouth snapping shut).
Row 1, Alley Rat: plump grey rat, big round pink ears, pink nose and long pink tail, buck teeth, sly grin, no clothes.
Row 2, Pot-Lid Rat: the same grey rat holding a big dented steel pot lid with a knob in front of its body like a round shield (the lid covers its front), peeking over it.
Row 3, Crow: glossy black crow with a yellow beak and white eye glint, walking on the ground; walk frames hop with wings slightly raised; bite frames peck forward with the beak.
Row 4, Tanuki: round chubby raccoon-dog, brown with a dark eye mask and dark legs, cream belly, striped fluffy tail, a green leaf on its head.
Row 5, Fox: slim orange kitsune fox with white chest and tail tip, big pointed ears with dark tips, sly narrow eyes, big bushy tail.
$STYLE No text, no numbers, no labels, no shadows, no ground, transparent background."

P_ITEMS="Game icon and prop sheet for a cozy Japanese noodle-house lane-defense game at night, transparent background, items widely separated by empty space, no text. Row 1 (four small icons, each simple and bold, readable at 16 pixels): (1) a shiny gold Japanese mon coin, round with a square hole in the centre, (2) a plump white steamed dumpling (gyoza bun) with pleats on top, (3) a round dented steel pot lid with a black knob, seen from the side at a slight tilt, (4) a glowing orange-red fire ember spark. Row 2 (four small icons): (5) a single glossy black crow feather, (6) a small grey puff of stone dust cloud, (7) a cream white dog bone, (8) a bright yellow five-pointed star with a white highlight. Row 3 (two larger sprites, same size): a small red noodle-delivery scooter facing RIGHT with a wooden bento box strapped on the back rack, round headlight, little wheels, no rider; (9) wheels in one position, (10) the same scooter with a small exhaust puff and wheels turned slightly (animation frame). $STYLE"

P_TILES="Four square seamless ground tiles for a top-down night garden lane-defense game, arranged in a 2 by 2 grid filling the whole image, each tile a perfect square filling exactly one quarter, seen straight from above (orthographic top-down), even lighting, no vignette, no shadows, no text, no objects. Top-left: a square grey flagstone paver set in short soft night-garden grass, the paver centred with an even grass margin all around. Top-right: plain short garden grass with a few tiny clover tufts, same green as the top-left. Bottom-left: warm honey-brown wooden porch deck planks running horizontally, plank seams and a few nail dots. Bottom-right: dark grey cobblestone alley paving with rounded stones and mossy cracks. Muted mid-tone night colors: dusky blue-green grass, cool grey stone, warm brown wood, nothing very dark and nothing very bright, low contrast so characters read on top. $STYLE"

P_HOUSE="Pixel-art background panel, a tall narrow vertical strip: the back wall of a small Japanese noodle house at night, straight-on flat front view, orthographic, no perspective, filling the whole image edge to edge. The important details are all within the CENTRAL HALF of the width: a dark wooden sliding back door with a cream noren curtain hanging over its top (the curtain has a simple bowl-of-noodles picture, no letters), two red paper lanterns hanging on either side of the door glowing warm, a small lit shoji window higher up, wooden timber frame posts and plum-dusky plaster, a dark tiled roof eave across the very top, a low stone step at the bottom. The outer quarters of the width are plain plaster wall and wooden posts that continue the wall. Warm lantern light, muted night tones so it stays a background. $STYLE No text, no letters."

P_ALLEY="Pixel-art background panel: a narrow Japanese back alley at night, straight-on flat front view, orthographic, no perspective, filling the whole image edge to edge. A tall old brick-and-plaster alley wall fills the upper area with a dark tiled wall cap at the very top; a string of small glowing red and orange paper lanterns swags across the top third; stacked wooden crates and a few barrels and a rain barrel stand against the wall along the lower sides; dark cobblestone ground at the bottom. The middle of the lower half stays fairly open and uncluttered (enemies walk through it). Muted dusky plum and blue-grey night tones with warm lantern glow, low contrast so characters read on top. $STYLE No text, no letters, no characters."

P_TITLE="Video game title logo that reads exactly \"SOBA GUARD\" (two words, all capitals, spelled S-O-B-A G-U-A-R-D) in big chunky blocky pixel-art lettering, 16-bit arcade style, on ONE line. Letters filled with a warm lantern gradient made of flat pixel bands (cream to gold to orange-red), a thick dark purple-black outline (#1a1220) and a darker plum drop shadow. A small cute pixel-art head of the dog from the reference image (black fluffy fur, tall pointed ears with pink insides, tan eyebrow dots, white muzzle, pink tongue out) peeks over the top of the letter O in SOBA. A small round red paper lantern hangs beside the word GUARD. The logo is centered and fills most of the frame on a perfectly flat, solid, pure green background (#00FF00) with nothing else on it: no gradient, no texture, no border, no other text."

P_HOUSE2="Pixel-art game background piece in a top-down RPG style (front wall seen straight on, roof seen from slightly above, like Stardew Valley buildings): a very TALL and very NARROW slice of the back of a small Japanese noodle house at night, about 3.5 times taller than wide, standing alone in the middle of the image on a transparent background, its left and right edges are straight vertical cuts. From top to bottom: a dark blue-grey tiled roof eave with a wooden gutter; a small glowing shoji window; plum-dusky plaster wall with dark wooden timber posts at both edges; one red paper lantern hanging on a bracket glowing warm; a narrow dark wooden sliding back door with a short cream noren curtain over its top (a simple bowl-of-noodles picture, no letters), door placed in the middle of the height; a second red lantern below; a low grey stone step and a strip of stone foundation at the very bottom. Warm lantern light, muted night tones so it stays a background. $STYLE No text, no letters."

P_ALLEY2="Pixel-art game background for a lane-defense game, top-down RPG style (high three-quarter view looking down, like Stardew Valley): the mouth of a narrow Japanese back alley at night where critters come in from the right. The TOP 12% of the image: a dark tiled wall cap and old brick-and-plaster alley wall with a string of small glowing red and orange paper lanterns swagged along it. The remaining 88% of the image: open dark cobblestone alley GROUND seen from above, mostly empty and uncluttered so characters can walk across it from right to left, with a few puddles reflecting lantern light, a drain grate, scattered leaves. Along the RIGHT edge only: a column of stacked wooden crates, a barrel and an overflowing trash bin. Muted dusky plum and blue-grey night tones with warm lantern glow, low contrast so characters read on top. $STYLE No text, no letters, no characters, no animals."

